WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.333 --> 00:00:05.467
I've spent my life around rockets.

2
00:00:05.467 --> 00:00:09.367
And every great leap I've seen was a team effort.

3
00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:14.567
Five agencies from fifteen nations run one space station together.

4
00:00:14.967 --> 00:00:18.200
But the way we work together has barely changed.

5
00:00:18.867 --> 00:00:22.800
Every partnership is still negotiated one treaty at a time.

6
00:00:23.033 --> 00:00:25.367
Designs stay behind export rules.

7
00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:27.867
Data sits in separate archives.

8
00:00:27.867 --> 00:00:30.867
And most of the world watches from outside.

9
00:00:31.667 --> 00:00:34.167
Then I saw SpaceDAO.

10
00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:38.333
A planetary space organization, run as a DAO:

11
00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:41.900
one open network where agencies, companies,

12
00:00:42.767 --> 00:00:45.367
scientists and funders plan missions together.

13
00:00:45.967 --> 00:00:48.167
Share technology as open blueprints.

14
00:00:48.733 --> 00:00:51.000
Share spare capacity on every rocket,

15
00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:53.667
so another nation's payload can ride along.

16
00:00:54.167 --> 00:00:56.067
Share the data that comes back.

17
00:00:56.433 --> 00:00:57.767
And decide together,

18
00:00:57.767 --> 00:01:01.533
with smart contracts that carry out what the council agrees.

19
00:01:02.333 --> 00:01:05.200
The more we connect, the farther we go.

20
00:01:05.867 --> 00:01:07.767
You can't build that in a weekend.

21
00:01:08.333 --> 00:01:10.500
So they built the experience of it:

22
00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:13.700
a game. And I couldn't stop playing.

23
00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:18.033
Pick a real mission, from the space station to the lunar south pole.

24
00:01:18.467 --> 00:01:19.667
Invite three partners.

25
00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:23.767
Design the rocket, the orbit and the spacecraft in 3D,

26
00:01:23.767 --> 00:01:26.767
while six gauges react to every choice.

27
00:01:27.567 --> 00:01:30.800
Before launch, your partners vote Go or No-Go.

28
00:01:31.267 --> 00:01:35.300
Only a unanimous Go unlocks a four-of-four multi-signature:

29
00:01:35.967 --> 00:01:39.200
a vault that opens only when all four keys turn.

30
00:01:39.633 --> 00:01:41.567
And those keys are quantum-safe:

31
00:01:42.167 --> 00:01:45.533
the new NIST standard, built to resist quantum computers

32
00:01:45.533 --> 00:01:47.000
in a web browser.

33
00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:50.833
In my day, that took a room full of lawyers.

34
00:01:51.467 --> 00:01:52.767
Then you fly.

35
00:01:53.467 --> 00:01:54.500
And here's what got me:

36
00:01:54.967 --> 00:01:57.200
the solar storms that hit you are real,

37
00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:59.000
from the last thirty days.

38
00:01:59.467 --> 00:02:00.100
On the Moon,

39
00:02:00.467 --> 00:02:04.033
your radio delay comes from today's real Earth-Moon distance.

40
00:02:04.567 --> 00:02:08.833
You survive the long lunar night, impacts and discoveries.

41
00:02:09.567 --> 00:02:13.367
Then the debrief tells you why it worked or why it failed.

42
00:02:13.767 --> 00:02:15.800
And your design joins the network,

43
00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:17.900
for the next mission to build on.

44
00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:22.033
Now picture what a blockchain gives an organization like this.

45
00:02:22.633 --> 00:02:23.333
Transparency:

46
00:02:23.467 --> 00:02:27.133
every decision on a permanent record no one can secretly rewrite.

47
00:02:27.833 --> 00:02:29.900
Privacy: with zero-knowledge proofs,

48
00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:34.333
a company can prove what it delivers without revealing its secrets.

49
00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:35.800
No tokens.

50
00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:36.900
No money.

51
00:02:37.333 --> 00:02:39.000
Just trust you can verify.

52
00:02:39.567 --> 00:02:42.200
All of it runs on live NASA data:

53
00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:47.300
solar storms, wildfires burning right now, the Deep Space Network.

54
00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:50.267
I've waited my whole life for this.

55
00:02:51.067 --> 00:02:52.700
Space belongs to humanity.

56
00:02:53.567 --> 00:02:54.767
Let's explore it together.

57
00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:56.267
Play SpaceDAO.
